## Lore

The Idie call themselves by a name from a language they no longer remember,
but most people know them as Swamp Men or Catfish People. They are stocky,
light gray humanoids with big fish-like eyes, catfish whiskers around the
mouth and chin, three webbed fingers on each hand and two webbed toes on
each foot. They live in the swamps, bayous, rivers and coasts of the
Southeast and along the Gulf of Mexico, with scattered villages up the
eastern seaboard as far as Nova Scotia.

Most Idie earn their living from the water, and they are widely held to be
the finest fishermen in the South. They prefer to fish with a spear out of
long tradition and plain enjoyment, not for lack of technology: they are as
handy with machines as any human, and many carry Vibro-Spears for big or
dangerous prey. Others build boats, run ferries, guide travelers through
the waterways, or take up piracy. Small family villages of a few dozen are
common, and many Idie live as valued members of human and D-Bee fishing
towns. They have adopted human culture as their own, keeping only a few old
customs, such as their spear fishing, their clothing and a week-long
seafood feast at the end of August to which everyone is welcome.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Coalition troops at Baton Rouge and Fort El Dorado call them Swamp Sushi.
Smuggling people past the Coalition naval base at Baton Rouge is said to
cost 3,000 to 5,000 credits a head.

Size 5 to 6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 m). Weight 150 to 320 pounds (67.5 to 144 kg).
Life span 2D6+65 years; mature by 17; females bear 1D4 live young after a
six month gestation, until about age 40. Slave market value 2D4x1,000
credits.

Most Idie avoid cybernetics and bionics.

Habitat: swamps, marshes, everglades, lakes, rivers and ocean coasts,
especially along the Gulf of Mexico; also Kentucky, Tennessee and the
eastern coastal states north to Nova Scotia. Coalition estimates put them at
about 130,000 in the Gulf States and 10,000 to 20,000 in the East.

Allies: most aquatic and amphibious D-Bees, especially Swamp Sludgers;
humans, Kraks and Horune Pirates; fair terms with the Natchez at Sky Fort
and the Crulls. Enemies: wary of Bayou Ursines and Larmac, and see the
Splugorth and their minions as evil enslavers.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'idie-swamp-man');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'idie-swamp-man';

